.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-captcha 1  "rev-stealth-captcha " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-captcha \- CAPTCHA bypass operations (reCAPTCHA v2 / v3 / hCaptcha / Turnstile)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth captcha\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
CAPTCHA resilience evaluation. Drives the captcha\-bypass solver against reCAPTCHA v2/v3, hCaptcha, or Turnstile, and verifies tokens via the provider\*(Aqs server\-side endpoint. AUTHORIZED TARGETS ONLY.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rev\-stealth\-captcha\-solve(1)
Solve a CAPTCHA challenge
.TP
rev\-stealth\-captcha\-verify(1)
Verify a previously\-issued token (round\-trips through the challenge provider\*(Aqs verify endpoint)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth captcha solve \-\-type recaptcha\-v2 \-\-site\-url https://example.com
  $ rev\-stealth captcha verify \-\-type hcaptcha \-\-token <TOKEN>

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Action completed.
  1  UserError        Bad args (unknown \-\-type / missing \-\-site\-url).
  2  TransientError   Solver or provider transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Solver not configured / challenge unsupported.

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_CAPTCHA_SECRET  Provider secret used by `captcha verify`.
